---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Security & responsible use — Bastco"
  description="How to approach authorized assessments, Kifaru’s operating boundaries, and sensitive security information when contacting Bastco."
>
  <div class="site-container">
    <article class="prose-page">
      <p class="eyebrow">Security &amp; responsible use</p><h1>
        Trust starts with<br />clear boundaries.
      </h1>
      <p>
        Security tools and services need an agreed scope, careful handling of
        evidence, and human review. This page explains operating expectations,
        not a certification or a guarantee of security.
      </p>
      <h2>Authorized assessments only</h2><p>
        Before an assessment, agree on the authorized targets, permitted
        activities, exclusions, and handling of findings. Do not use Bastco’s
        tools against systems you do not have permission to assess.
      </p>
      <h2>Kifaru’s execution boundary</h2><p>
        Kifaru is a Bastco security assessment agent that runs tools on the
        local host. A target selection, working directory, action permission, or
        Python environment is <strong
          >not a filesystem or network sandbox</strong
        >. The local dashboard’s authentication does not isolate agent
        execution.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use trusted workspaces and review requested actions.</li><li>
          Do not treat the workbench as an isolated, untrusted multi-tenant
          service.
        </li><li>
          Model-generated findings need independent review and reproduction.
        </li><li>
          Headless usage budgets react to reported consumption. They are not
          guaranteed provider-side spending caps.
        </li><li>
          Review model-provider settings and data-handling requirements before
          supplying sensitive assessment context.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        See the <a href="/kifaru">Kifaru overview</a> and <a
          href="https://install.bastco.org"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">installation instructions</a
        > before getting started.
      </p>
      <h2>Sharing security concerns</h2><p>
        Please don’t send credentials, personal data, exploit payloads, or
        vulnerability evidence through a scheduling form. <a href="/#contact"
          >Arrange a conversation with Bastco</a
        > to establish a suitable private reporting channel before sending sensitive
        details.
      </p><p>
        This website does not publish a bounty program or a reporting SLA.
        Publicly available information is not permission to test production systems.
      </p>
      <h2>This website</h2><p>
        The public site is statically generated. The scheduling calendar is
        optional and loaded only after you activate it. See <a href="/privacy"
          >website privacy</a
        > for the distinction between this site and third-party scheduling.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
